{title: 051 - Day Is Dying in the West}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #051 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 51}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Day is [C]dying [G]in the west; Heaven is touching earth with rest;
[D7]Wait and [G]worship [D7]while the [G]night [D7]Sets her [G]evening [A7]lamps a[Bm]light
[G]Through [D]all [A7]the [D]sky.
[G]Holy, holy, holy, Lord [D7]God of [G]hosts! [C]Heaven and earth are [G]full of Thee;
[D7]Heaven and earth are [G]praising Thee, [C]O [G]Lord [D7]most [G]high!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G]Holy, holy, [C]holy, Lord [G]God of Hosts!
[D7][G]Heaven [D7]and [G]earth [D7]are [G]full [A7]of [Bm]Thee!
[G]Heaven [D]and earth [A7]are [D]praising Thee,
[G][D7]O [G]Lord [C]most [G]high!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Lord of [C]life, beneath [G]the dome
[D7][G]Of [D7][G]the [D7]universe, [G][A7]Thy [Bm]home,
[G]Gather [D]us who [A7]seek [D]Thy face
[G]To [D7]the [G]fold [C]of [G]Thy embrace,
[D7][G]For [C]Thou [G][D7]art [G]nigh.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]While [C]the deepening [G]shadows fall,
[D7][G]Heart [D7][G]of [D7]love [G][A7]enfolding [Bm]all,
[G]Through [D]the glory [A7]and [D]the grace
[G]Of [D7]the [G]stars that [C]veil [G]Thy face,
[D7][G]Our [C][G]hearts [D7][G]ascend.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]When [C]forever from [G]our sight
[D7][G]Pass [D7]the [G]stars, [D7]the [G]day, [A7]the [Bm]night,
[G]Lord [D]of angels, [A7]on [D]our eyes
[G][D7]Let [G]eternal [C]morning [G]rise
[D7][G]And [C][G]shadows [D7][G]end.
{end_of_verse}
